{#
  An intermediary step between "View" on manage-guidance/document-
  overview.html and the guidance viewer itself — lets a reviewer pick a
  viewer layout rather than "View" going straight to one. See
  controller.js's own top comment for the two destinations' exact routes.

  Native govukRadios + Continue, not the earlier card-based version
  (.app-card) — the task asked for the standard GDS radio-button pattern
  ("Where do you live?") instead, so a real <form method="post"> is
  needed here now: choosing an option no longer navigates directly, it
  selects a radio, and Continue is what submits to controller.js's own
  post, which validates a selection was made and redirects to the chosen
  viewer. Validation follows the same govukErrorSummary pattern already
  established for a radios-with-Continue page in this codebase (app/
  views/v6/create-guidance/page.njk + its controller): errors.viewer =
  { text, href }, errorList: Object.values(errors), the same template
  re-rendered with the selection preserved on failure, novalidate on the
  form since the server-side check is what actually runs.

  Breadcrumbs (Home > <guidance title>), not a Back link — GOV.UK
  guidance is not to use both on the same page, same choice every other
  breadcrumb-bearing page in this app already makes. The breadcrumb is
  this page's only mention of which guidance it's about — no separate
  "Title" caption/heading repeating it in the body. Extends common/
  layouts/base.njk directly and hand-rolls its own grid, not common/
  layouts/content.njk — that layout's single two-thirds column has no
  room above it for a full-width breadcrumb row, the same reason manage-
  guidance/document-overview.html and saved-document-view.html both do
  the same thing.

  The fieldset legend itself is this page's <h1> (isPageHeading: true,
  the same technique create-guidance/page.njk uses) rather than a
  separate heading above the radios — GOV.UK's own radios pattern always
  treats the question being asked as the page heading when the radios
  are the whole page. The explanatory paragraph becomes the fieldset's
  own hint text, rendered directly under that heading and above the
  options, which is exactly what a fieldset hint is for.

  Both destinations carry the guidance id through in their own URL, both
  under /v6/find-guidance/ (/v6/find-guidance/document/<id> — the real
  step-by-step guidance viewer — and /v6/find-guidance/document-
  experiment/<id> — a single-page layout being trialled alongside it,
  still fixed placeholder content regardless of which id reaches it) —
  see controller.js's own top comment for exactly what each renders.
#}
{% extends "common/layouts/base.njk" %}

{% from "govuk/components/breadcrumbs/macro.njk" import govukBreadcrumbs %}
{% from "govuk/components/radios/macro.njk" import govukRadios %}
{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}
{% from "govuk/components/error-summary/macro.njk" import govukErrorSummary %}

{% set pageName = "Choose how you'd like to view this guidance" %}
{% if errorList and errorList.length %}{% set pageName = "Error: " + pageName %}{% endif %}

{% block content %}

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-full">
    {{ govukBreadcrumbs({
      classes: "govuk-!-margin-bottom-6",
      items: [
        { text: "Home", href: "/consolidated/hub" },
        { text: documentTitle }
      ]
    }) }}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">

    {% if errorList and errorList.length %}
      {{ govukErrorSummary({ titleText: "There is a problem", errorList: errorList }) }}
    {% endif %}

    <form method="post" action="/consolidated/document/{{ id }}/view" novalidate>

      {{ govukRadios({
        idPrefix: "guidance-viewer",
        name: "viewer",
        value: selected,
        fieldset: {
          legend: {
            text: "Choose how you'd like to view this guidance",
            isPageHeading: true,
            classes: "govuk-fieldset__legend--l"
          }
        },
        hint: {
          text: "Two ways to view this guidance are available while a new layout is being tried out. Pick either one — you can come back and try the other at any time."
        },
        errorMessage: errors.viewer,
        items: [
          {
            value: "stepper",
            text: "Stepper format",
            hint: { text: "The current guidance viewer layout." }
          },
          {
            value: "traditional",
            text: "Traditional viewer",
            hint: { text: "A new layout being tried out for viewing guidance." }
          }
        ]
      }) }}

      {{ govukButton({ text: "Continue" }) }}

    </form>

  </div>
</div>

{% endblock %}
